<text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
  <body>
    <div rend="parallel"> 
      <p xml:id="Aink170-kilavi">
        talaimakaṟkup puṟattoḻukka muḷatākiyavaḻi vēṟupaṭṭa talaimakaḷ avaṟku avvāṟu nikaḻicciyillai; nammēl aṉpuṭaiyaṉ eṉṟu teḷikkuntōḻikkuc colliyatu.'.</p>    <p xml:lang="en">
           Spoken by the heroine, who changed [her mind about him] when the hero lived with other women, to the confidante who clarified, saying 'nothing of that kind took place; he has love for us'.</p>
  </div>  
    <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="Aink170">
<l>peruṅkaṭaṟ karaiyatu ciṟuveṇ kākkai</l>
<l>yiruṅkaḻi neytal citaikkun tuṟaiva</l>
<l>ṉalla ṉeṉṟi yāyiṟ</l>
<l>pallita ḻuṇkaṇ pacattaṉmaṟ ṟevaṉō</l>
      </lg>
      <lg xml:lang="en">
        <l>If you say</l>
        <l>The man from the shore - in which the small, white crow of the vast seashore</l>
        <l>Scatters the Neytal flower in the dark backwaters - is a good man,</l>
        <l>Why indeed is there paling in my kajal-lined eyes [that are like] many petals? </l>      </lg>
    </div>
  </body>
</text>
